This is an introduction to techniques for quickly improving the score of the sit-and-reach flexibility test.

**1. Stretching Exercises**:
- Standing Forward Bend: Keep your feet together, legs straight, bend forward to touch the ground, hold for 30–60 seconds, repeat 3–5 sets. For advanced stretching, hug your calves;
- Seated Forward Bend with Legs Apart: Sit on the ground with legs straight and apart, lean forward and reach for your toes, hold for 30–60 seconds, repeat 3–5 sets;
- Cross-Legged Forward Bend: Sit cross-legged with the soles of your feet together, lean forward to touch your chest, hold for 30–60 seconds, repeat 3–5 sets;
- Supine Stretch: Lie flat, lift your leg and hug it, hold for 15–20 seconds, repeat 3–5 times.
**2. Core Strength Training**: Plank exercise, place your hands shoulder-width apart on the ground and keep your feet together.

